@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · 环境要求：- DeepSeek Harness Desktop 或 Web `0.2.1-rc.x`，`@deepseek-ai/cordis` 4.0.5；
- Node.js ≥ 22.19；
- 本机可用 Git（以 `github:` 方式安装时）。

@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · 从 npm 安装（推荐）：```bash
dsh plugin --profile desktop add @whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace
```

@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · 开发：本轮的每一条安全修复都做过**变异自检**：把实现改回旧行为，对应测试必须变红。改完安全相关的代码后建议照做一遍——只加 happy-path 用例而不做这一步，很容易得到"看起来被守护、实际删掉也全绿"的测试（第二轮审查 56 次变异里仍有 21 次存活，见 `review/REVIEW-2026-10-27-round2.md`）。

本轮的 6 条行为修复各自都有守护测试，并且都用变异法复核过：`orderBy` 回退成"未列出的一律后置"、`samePath` 回退成严格相等、隐式新会话回退成归入最新分组、跨工作区护栏去掉、marquee 回退成来回摆、以及死区阈值归零——每一条都会让对应测试变红。

> 变异脚本本身也要验证：第一版因为工作区是 CRLF（`\n}\n` 锚点匹配不到）与注入点落在 `continue` 之后，曾报出两个**假绿**。现在脚本会先确认锚点命中、变异后仍能构建、并且目标测试确实**跑过并失败**，否则记为"检查无效"而不是通过。改代码后若要复跑这类自检，请照这三条来核对，不要只看脚本打印的 ok。

@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · dsh-better-workspace：- **Topic groups** — one tree per workspace, with emoji-marked "group" folders holding sessions, plus a system default group and an Archived bucket;
- **Filter and search** — a workspace dropdown, in-panel local search, and "only this group";
- **Bulk actions** — archive / unarchive / move to group / permanent delete, carried by a single row of native icon buttons in the header while selection mode is on;
- **Safe deletion** — DSH has no host-side delete command, so the plugin implements one, and the rule is "refuse rather than risk it" (see [Deletion safety boundaries](#deletion-safety-boundaries));
- **Native look** — status dots, pinning that actually floats rows up, hover cards, row hover actions, scheduled-task clock marks, icons and colors all follow the host's own implementation.

@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · Requirements：- DeepSeek Harness Desktop or Web `0.2.1-rc.x`, `@deepseek-ai/cordis` 4.0.5;
- Node.js ≥ 22.19;
- Git available locally (for the `github:` install path).

@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · Sessions：- **Double-click** to rename (same as the desktop app);
- **Hover** for the native hover card: full title, relative time, idle/working/waiting status, and an archived marker when archived;
- **Hover a clipped title**: like the native list, it crawls to its far edge at ~30 px/s and **rests there** (no bounce, no back-and-forth); leaving returns it to the start at once. Overflow under 8 px is left alone (it would read as jitter), and reduced-motion jumps straight to the end;
- **Row hover** reveals `⋯ / archive / pin`, with the inline timestamp yielding to them;
- **Drag** — onto another workspace is refused (guard); onto another group files the session there. While dragging, the other groups of the workspace fold away (the source topic stays open for in-group reordering), so a distant group only needs its header as the target;
- **Pin** actually floats the row to the top of its group (host pin order, most recent first).

@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · Where a new session lands：- A workspace row's ＋ and the rail's "new session" leave the session with **no group assignment written**, so it stays in the system default group and sorts first inside that bucket — the same placement the official list gives it;
- The header ＋ → "new session" picks a workspace and a group (the default group is in the list too), then creates the session and files it into that choice;
- A group row's ＋, or an explicitly chosen group in the ＋ flow: the session is created and then filed into that group;
- Creating one while "only this group" is active files it into that group, since it is the place you are looking at; the write happens only when the new blank really belongs to that workspace, so a blank started by another window in a different workspace is never re-filed;
- Forking: the child joins the group its source sits in — from the row menu, the stock fork shortcut, or the chat view's branch command. The tree projects it there directly, so it **never flashes in the default group** before jumping; the written assignment only makes that placement persist. A source already in the default group writes nothing, and t

@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · Bulk actions：- Mixing **archived** rows into the selection disables archive and move; mixing **unarchived** rows disables unarchive; mixing **ungrouped** sessions disables move;
- The toolbar states the reason below the row, and hovering shows the same;
- The provisional "new session" row never joins a selection;
- **"Select all" only spans the rows on screen**: the group checkbox, the topic ⋯ menu and the workspace ⋯ menu all consume one derivation (`selectableIds`), so a bucket past "show all 60" reports "selected N; M more are not shown yet" and asks you to expand it — it never quietly pulls rows that were never rendered into a batch permanent delete;
- A session removed by another window drops out of the batch targets instead of failing the whole batch with "no such session";
- Leaving selection mode clears the selection.

@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · Permanent deletion：- A running session is stopped the official way (`agent.cancel({kind:'user'})`) and given up to 3 seconds to leave `running`; if it does not, nothing is deleted;
- A session with subagent children is refused — delete the parent instead (children are cascaded and counted in the preview);
- A user fork (with `parentSession` but no `origin`) is a top-level session: it deletes on its own and is never treated as a subagent;
- Deleting the session you are viewing switches to a fresh blank session.

@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · Workspace membership repair：- a workspace was deleted and re-created (`sessionIds` went with the old record);
- the host crashed or the window closed between the header write and `attachSession`;
- the session was resumed through a different path (for example reusing an older blank record).

@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · Deletion safety boundaries：1. The session id must be a single safe path segment (no `/`, `\`, `..`);
2. The directory must live under `<DSH_HOME>/sessions`, with every path level checked via `lstat` + `realpath`, rejecting symlinks/junctions; a sessions root that is itself a link is refused outright;
3. The first line (header) of `session.v3.jsonl[.zstd]` must be read and confirm `header.id === sessionId` — a directory-name match alone never deletes;
4. A session whose artifact was **appended to recently** is blocked (subagent sessions are blocked too, and are cascaded by their parent with a count in the preview; **an orphaned subagent whose parent artifact is gone is the exception** — the cascade entry point no longer exists, so it may be deleted on its own, otherwise the file would stay on disk forever); a user fork carrying only `parentSession` is not a subagent. Note that DSH's write lease is *not* "a lock file exists": Windows uses a named kernel semaphore, and on POSIX `session.lock` is never removed once created — so this checks the artifact's recent modification time (a 3-second quiet window when the host has positively confirmed the

@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · Switching off and rollback：- **Temporarily disable** — set the plugin's `config.enabled` to `false` in the profile's `cordis.patch.yml`; after a restart the official UI is fully restored;
- **Disable deletion only** — `config.enableDelete: false` (routes return 403, and the batch toolbar hides the delete button);
- **Uninstall** — see Uninstalling above; topic data stays in `<DSH_HOME>/dsh-better-workspace/`.

@whybebabo/dsh-better-workspace README · Known limits：- The **workspace** order is stored in local preferences only, so it is not shared across windows (group order is);
- The official Workspace header's search/sort buttons are covered; the panel provides its own local search (local matching, not the remote `sessions.search`);
- The session row menu is drawn by the plugin (it cannot borrow the official entry, see above), but order, wording, icons and shortcut hints match the original item by item; hints come from the host's current default bindings, so rebinding them in settings leaves the hint text stale (the action itself still goes through official commands);
- The group row's ＋ "new session" relies on the host marking new sessions as `blank`; if a future version stops doing that it degrades to "not auto-filed" (still movable), never to modifying existing sessions;
- Permanent deletion depends on host-internal service names (`sessions`/`agents`/`workspaceRegistry`/`storageDomain` with `session_projcache` and `workspace`), which need re-checking on every DSH major version; if a cleanup service is missing the log is still deleted and failures are recorded in the result;
